---
<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 3.2 · Varlamore, Wyrmscraig & Runecraft" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="3-2" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 3.2</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Varlamore, Wyrmscraig &amp; Runecraft</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Let quest XP do the heavy lifting: fight the Moons, visit modern Wyrmscraig, and step Runecraft through 47 → 50 → 52 → 55 while quests repeatedly shrink the next gap.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Perilous Moons → Heart of Darkness → Slayer 60 → Runecraft 47 → Fallen From Grace → Crafting 65 → Runecraft 50 → Devious Minds → Runecraft 52 → Final Dawn → Runecraft 55 → Fremennik Exiles."
        stats={["Read live XP after every quest; train only to the next actual gate", "Actual 60 Slayer, 65 Crafting and 55 Runecraft before The Fremennik Exiles", "No Runecraft 60, Slayer 69 or Crafting 70 grind on this page"]}
        unlocks={["Neypotzli and its first normal Lunar Chest reward", "Wyrmscraig, Tapoyauik and the Varlamore finale", "Island of Stone and V's shield"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>3.1 handoff—read, do not assume exact XP.</strong> The mandatory route brings actual 58+ Slayer, 67+ Magic, 60+ Strength, WGS, 70 Prayer/Defence and Piety; Barrows gloves, dragon defender, Helm of Neitiznot and Proselyte; approximately 63+ Crafting and 38+ Runecraft; 67+ Sailing, 71+ Mining, 70+ Smithing and 74+ Fishing; Twilight's Promise, Children of the Sun, Pandemonium and a camphor-hulled skiff. WGS's Thieving/Farming/Herblore/Hunter rewards have landed. Check the live skill tab and bank before using any conservative floor. No black mask or Bowfa is presumed.</div>
      <div class="callout"><strong>Runecraft rule:</strong> train to the <em>next actual gate</em> → do the quest → claim its XP → read live XP again. Perilous Moons, Fallen From Grace, Devious Minds, The Final Dawn and The Fremennik Exiles supply <strong>5,000 + 5,000 + 5,000 + 25,000 + 30,000 = 70,000 fixed Runecraft XP</strong> across this page. None can satisfy its own entry gate. The future actual-60 gate belongs beside its later consumer, not here.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Varlamore · two stories, then a tiny Slayer bridge</div><h2>Take the large quest rewards before training.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i32-moons" number="1" title="Complete Perilous Moons and claim one normal Lunar Chest reward">
        <p><strong>Entry audit:</strong> actual 48 Slayer, 20 Hunter, 20 Fishing, 20 Runecraft, 10 Construction and Twilight's Promise are all behind the route. Go to the <strong>Cam Torum entrance on the south side of Ralos' Rise</strong> in Varlamore; use your existing Varlamore access to reach the region, then follow the Cam Torum path into <strong>Neypotzli</strong>. Speak to Zuma/Attala at the entrance to begin. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Perilous_Moons" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest requirements and rewards</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>First trip:</strong> bring the banked dragon scimitar, dragon defender, Barrows gloves, Helm of Neitiznot, your best <em>defensive</em> melee armour, food and a teleport. Neypotzli has campsite crates, fishing and hunting resources, cooking stoves, and moonlight grubs to turn into moonlight potions, so the ordinary loop is <strong>gather/cook food → make potions → fight each Moon → open the chest</strong>. Moonlight potions restore Prayer and boost combat; protection prayers <strong>do not reduce the Moon bosses' attacks</strong>. Their three-hit sequences punish poor defence, so defensive armour and learning the special phases matter more than a rare damage upgrade. Piety is useful, but not a substitute for movement. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Moons_of_Peril/Strategies" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current encounter strategy</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="The three Moons, using attainable weapons" label="Boss primer">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Blood Moon—slash:</strong> use the dragon scimitar and defender. Hits on you heal her; prioritize defence, follow Eyatlalli's highlighted safe circle, move off raining-blood pools and work the highlighted blood-jaguar phase rather than trying to out-DPS mistakes.</li>
            <li><strong>Blue Moon—crush:</strong> a <strong>dragon mace</strong> is a deterministic, buyable crush swap after Heroes' Quest (Heroes' Guild); if you already have a reasonable crush weapon, use it. Punch the ice block to recover your frozen weapon while avoiding spikes; during the other special, relight both braziers while avoiding tornadoes.</li>
            <li><strong>Eclipse Moon—stab:</strong> use a banked stab-capable weapon, including the dragon dagger if owned; the dragon scimitar can still finish the quest if no special swap is available. Keep the moving moon shield between you and the boss during the ray phase, and face each spawning clone during the mimic phase.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>You can leave and restock between encounters. No Barrows set, Moon gear or Bowfa is required.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>Defeat all three as the quest directs and collect its <strong>one normal Lunar Chest reward</strong>. Claim <strong>40,000 Slayer, 5,000 Runecraft, 5,000 Hunter and 5,000 Fishing XP</strong>. Bank any Moon unique, including an Eclipse atlatl, as a welcome bonus; <strong>do not farm a set</strong>. At the exact actual-58 Slayer floor, <strong>224,466 + 40,000 = 264,466 XP</strong>, leaving <strong>9,276 XP</strong> to level 60 <em>before</em> the next quest's Slayer reward. Read live XP; do not train yet.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-heart" number="2" title="Complete The Heart of Darkness while in Varlamore">
        <p>Begin with <strong>Prince Itzla at the Teomat</strong>. The actual 55 Mining, 48 Thieving, 48 Slayer and 46 Agility gates, plus Twilight's Promise, are already covered; Perilous Moons is not a direct prerequisite, but both stories are required later for The Final Dawn. Investigate the cult, travel into the icy ruins of <strong>Tapoyauik</strong> and defeat <strong>Amoxliatl</strong>. Bring melee gear, the dragon mace/defender if purchased, Protect from Magic, food and an emergency teleport. During the fight, move off persistent ice, destroy unstable ice blocks with melee before they burst/heal her, and reactivate Protect from Magic when her icicle attack switches Prayer off. This is a story/area-unlock quest, <strong>not</strong> a request to farm Amoxliatl. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Heart_of_Darkness" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest walkthrough and rewards</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Amoxliatl/Strategies" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Fight mechanics</a>.</p>
        <p>Claim <strong>8,000 XP each in Mining, Thieving, Slayer and Agility</strong> and the Tapoyauik access. The Slayer reward is easy to overlook: at the exact 58 floor, <strong>224,466 + 40,000 + 8,000 = 272,466 XP</strong>. Against the <strong>273,742-XP</strong> level-60 gate, that leaves at most <strong>1,276 XP</strong> before Duradel's notes or incidental tasks.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-slayer-60" number="3" title="Finish only the live remainder to actual 60 Slayer">
        <p>Read Slayer XP <strong>after both Varlamore quest rewards</strong> and any already-used Duradel's notes. At the conservative exact-58 floor, the remaining gap is at most <strong>1,276 XP</strong>; for most real accounts it may already be zero. If short, complete ordinary Slayer assignments through an eligible master and stop at <strong>actual 60</strong>. The optional Chapter 3.1 black mask can be worn if it dropped; otherwise nothing changes. Actual 60 is consumed by <strong>The Fremennik Exiles</strong>. Slayer 69 belongs later, after Exiles' 50,000-XP reward.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Runecraft · first measured interval</div><h2>One gate, then an island quest.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i32-rc-47" number="4" title="Reach actual 47 Runecraft after the Moon reward">
        <p>Read live Runecraft XP after Perilous Moons' <strong>5,000 XP</strong>. The conservative Chapter 2/3.1 floor was about <strong>33,210 XP</strong>; now about <strong>38,210 XP</strong>. Level 47 begins at <strong>75,127 XP</strong>, so the exact-floor training remainder is approximately <strong>36,917 XP</strong>, less any other live XP. Stop at <strong>actual 47</strong>, the Fallen From Grace entry gate.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i32-rc-methods" skill="Runecraft" target="the next live gate only" why="Use the same ordinary method in later short returns, each time after claiming the preceding quest XP." recommended="Guardians of the Rift: gather fragments, make guardian essence, enter opened altars, craft runes, then use charged cells to reinforce barriers or make guardians. Balance elemental/catalytic energy for reward searches; no fletching or gem-cutting detour." relaxed="Sins of the Father already opens the Daeyalt mine in Darkmeyer. Mine shards with longer, quieter clicks; exchange them for banked essence, then use it at Ourania/ZMI. The altar laps still need attention, so this is lower-attention overall, not AFK Runecraft." informational={true} />
        <p><strong>GOTR refresher:</strong> return to the Temple of the Eye beneath the Wizards' Tower (completed in Chapter 1), enter the Rift, mine guardian fragments, convert them at the workbench, and take essence through whichever rune altar portal is open. Deposit crafted guardian stones into the Great Guardian and place charged cells in barrier/guardian positions so the rift closes. Earn elemental and catalytic points and search the Rewards Guardian between games. Keep any essence pouches from reward searches. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Guardians_of_the_Rift" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Minigame and reward mechanics</a>. For a quieter split, <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ourania_Altar" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Ourania</a> is west of the Battlefield: bring pure/daeyalt essence and 20 expendable runes per bank access, use the longer safe east path if desired, then craft mixed runes at its altar. Mining Daeyalt is the relaxed portion; the bank/altar loop is not truly AFK. Do not farm a pouch early solely for Step 8.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-fallen" number="5" title="Complete Fallen From Grace using your own camphor skiff">
        <p><strong>Hard gate:</strong> actual 62 Sailing, 60 Crafting, <strong>47 Runecraft</strong>, 53 Mining and Pandemonium. The route covers all but the gate just trained. Sail your <strong>own raft or skiff—not a sloop</strong> to <strong>Wyrmscraig</strong>, south-west of Charred Island. The Chapter 2 <strong>camphor-hulled skiff</strong> already works. Wyrmscraig is a newer player-designed island; the main settlement is <strong>Auchrie</strong>. Speak with <strong>Cormac in its central hut</strong> and follow the missing-villager/sunstone investigation. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Fallen_From_Grace" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current quest guide</a>.</p>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Bank before departure:</strong> you cannot use a Wyrmscraig bank or teleport to the island until the quest is complete. Bring melee gear, a <strong>crush</strong> option such as the Heroes' Guild dragon mace, food, Prayer/restore supplies and a return teleport before sailing; leave room for quest items. A pickaxe, hammer and chisel can be found during the investigation, but bring yours if banked. You can sail back to restock if needed—just budget the return crossing.</div>
        <p>Investigate the monolith and cavern, defeat the three trolls (Protect from Melee helps in their multicombat area), solve the cathedral trail and face the <strong>weaker quest version of the Mad Angel</strong>. It is a mechanics fight: use crush and Protect from Melee for ordinary attacks, move through/behind her telegraphed sword sweep, step onto the marked shadows to redirect the yellow orb, and switch to Protect from Magic for the blue lightning. This is not the repeatable post-quest boss farm. Claim <strong>12,500 Sailing, 10,000 Crafting, 5,000 Mining and 5,000 Runecraft XP</strong> plus Wyrmscraig travel, Golem Crafting, Mortimer's Slayer-master access and the repeatable Mad Angel unlock.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="What can wait on Wyrmscraig" label="Optional after the quest">
          <p><strong>Hallowfell</strong> is an equipment branch from the repeat boss, not a Quest Cape prerequisite. <strong>Sunstone Golem Crafting</strong> is another Crafting method; banked materials can finish our much smaller 65 gate. <strong>Mortimer</strong> offers Slayer assignments if eligible, but no task from him is required here. Record these unlocks and leave the island without farming Mad Angel drops.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-craft-65" number="6" title="Reach actual 65 Crafting after Fallen From Grace">
        <p>Read live Crafting XP <strong>after Fallen's 10,000 XP</strong>. At the conservative actual-63 floor, <strong>368,599 + 10,000 = 378,599 XP</strong>; actual 65 begins at <strong>449,428 XP</strong>, a maximum floor-case remainder of <strong>70,829 XP</strong>. Use the materials actually banked; the player's number may be much smaller. Actual 65 is consumed by <strong>The Fremennik Exiles</strong>. Do <strong>not</strong> pretrain to 70 for Monkey Madness II: Exiles itself pays 50,000 Crafting XP.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i32-craft-methods" skill="Crafting" target="actual 65" why="Apply Fallen's 10,000 first and stop before Exiles' 50,000 reward." recommended="Blow banked molten glass into useful lantern lenses or other available products; use banked gems and battlestaff materials where they make sense." relaxed="For fresh glass, gather/buy buckets of sand and soda ash or cook seaweed, combine one of each at a furnace, then use a glassblowing pipe. Make only enough for the live XP gap; no giant-seaweed stock is assumed." informational={true} />
        <p><strong>Spellbook check:</strong> Superglass Make requires <strong>77 Magic</strong>; the route currently guarantees only actual 67+, so do not assume it. Ordinary furnace glassmaking works now. Reserve <strong>one molten glass</strong> for The Fremennik Exiles if one is not already banked.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-rc-50" number="7" title="Reach actual 50 Runecraft, then secure the quest pouch">
        <p>Read live Runecraft XP after Fallen's <strong>5,000 XP</strong>. If Step 4 stopped exactly at 47's <strong>75,127 XP</strong>, you now have at least <strong>80,127 XP</strong>; level 50 begins at <strong>101,333 XP</strong>, so the floor-case remainder is <strong>21,206 XP</strong>. Return to your chosen ordinary method and stop at <strong>actual 50</strong>. Do not train to 52 before Devious Minds pays its XP.</p>
        <p><strong>Mandatory pouch preflight:</strong> check bank and inventory for a <strong>non-degraded large essence pouch or colossal pouch</strong>. If absent, first search any saved GOTR reward pulls. Pouch drops follow ownership progression: hold a <strong>small pouch</strong> (the Abyss dark mage can give one), then <strong>medium</strong>, then <strong>large</strong>—check the bank after each. Temple of the Eye may already have supplied the medium. GOTR's Rewards Guardian can award pouches naturally; alternatively, fairy ring <strong>ALR</strong> reaches the Abyssal Area <em>without a Wilderness crossing</em>. Kill ordinary Abyssal walkers/guardians there with combat gear, food and teleport until the missing next pouch drops. The August 2026 improvement raised pouch rolls to <strong>up to 1/5 per walker</strong> or <strong>up to 1/8 per guardian</strong> (formerly 1/42); those are <em>odds, not a guaranteed number of kills</em>. You do not need the pouch's use level to obtain it. Repair a degraded large pouch through the dark mage before the quest. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Essence_pouch" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Pouch order and sources</a> · <a href="https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/summer-sweep-up---agility--chambers-of-xeric-changes?oldschool=1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Jagex's August 2026 pouch-rate update</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Classic detour · then back to Varlamore</div><h2>Each quest makes the next Runecraft interval shorter.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i32-devious" number="8" title="Complete Devious Minds and claim 5,000 Runecraft XP">
        <p>Check <strong>actual 50 Runecraft</strong> (not boostable), 65 Smithing, 50 Fletching, Wanted!, Troll Stronghold/Death Plateau, Doric's Quest and Enter the Abyss. The route covers these. Obtain a <strong>mithril two-handed sword</strong> (buy from <strong>Gaius in Taverley</strong> or smith it), <strong>bow string</strong> and the <strong>non-degraded large or colossal pouch</strong>. Speak to the monk outside Paterdomus, use Doric's whetstone on the sword, attach the string and follow the orb/Entrana phase. The sword and string are consumed. A normal large pouch is consumed; a colossal pouch survives. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Devious_Minds/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current item and phase guide</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Ironman travel warning:</strong> bank weapons and armour for Entrana before the Law Altar trip. The quest's Abyss entry via the Mage of Zamorak crosses <strong>level 4–7 Wilderness</strong>; ALR is useful for <em>pouch farming</em> but does not replace this quest phase. A Hardcore Ironman should treat the crossing as real PvP risk: travel light, check the world, and use a teleport/escape plan. Do not insert the orb into the pouch before you are ready for that phase; losing it can require recovery. Finish with Sir Tiffy and claim <strong>5,000 Runecraft, 5,000 Fletching and 6,500 Smithing XP</strong>. This also closes a later Secrets of the North / Desert Treasure II prerequisite.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-rc-52" number="9" title="Reach actual 52 Runecraft after Devious Minds">
        <p>Read live XP after Devious Minds' <strong>5,000 RC XP</strong>. At an exact-50 training stop, <strong>101,333 + 5,000 = 106,333 XP</strong>. Level 52 begins at <strong>123,660 XP</strong>, so the floor-case training remainder is <strong>17,327 XP</strong>. Use the method that still feels tolerable, then stop at <strong>actual 52</strong>: The Final Dawn consumes it and awards a much larger 25,000 XP. No early 55 grind.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-dawn" number="10" title="Complete The Final Dawn and claim its 25,000 Runecraft XP">
        <p><strong>Gate audit:</strong> Perilous Moons and The Heart of Darkness complete; actual <strong>66 Thieving, 52 Runecraft and 52 Fletching</strong>. WGS and Chapter 2 already cleared the non-RC levels. Start with <strong>Servius in the Sunrise Palace</strong>. Keep the emissary robes from Heart (reclaim as the quest allows), a knife and ordinary food/combat supplies; bones or meat and beer can be obtained as the phases direct. This is a long Varlamore story/fight sequence, so <strong>bank and regear between phases</strong> instead of hauling every item at once. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Final_Dawn" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest and combat walkthrough</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Combat preflight: several encounters, two different finales" label="Fight plan">
          <p>Use the existing dragon scimitar/defender, Helm of Neitiznot, Barrows gloves, defensive armour, Piety, Prayer/restore potions, good food, an emergency teleport, and a <strong>real banked Ranged weapon with ammunition</strong> plus Ava's accumulator. No Bowfa, Eclipse atlatl, Moon set, black mask, Fire Cape or Rigour is required; a Moon drop is merely a bonus.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Emissary Enforcer, Chimalli/Lucius and cultist waves:</strong> expect multiple fights, changing threats and ground/projectile mechanics. Protect against the active attack style, move from telegraphs, clear adds and restock when a phase ends.</li>
            <li><strong>Ennius Tullus:</strong> he has <strong>Protect from Ranged and Magic simultaneously</strong>, so this is a <strong>melee</strong> fight. Keep a protection prayer up for his ordinary attacks and step onto the safe circles/away from marked sunfire attacks; do not waste supplies trying to range through his prayers.</li>
            <li><strong>Augur Metzli:</strong> now Ranged is useful. She starts in a ranged-attacking form, later alternates Ranged/Magic after sweeper attacks; switch the matching protection prayer and move through safe rows/columns or white portals for waves and sweepers. During the final quadrant/fire phase, keep moving through the portal to the safe quadrant while attacking when possible. Prince Itzla assists, but you still handle your own mechanics.</li>
          </ul>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>Finish and claim <strong>55,000 Thieving, 25,000 Runecraft and 25,000 Fletching XP</strong>, plus the selectable <strong>55,000 combat-XP lamp</strong> (a skill of at least level 40, including Prayer), the <strong>Arkan blade</strong> and access to the Crypt of Tonali/Doom of Mokhaiotl. Choose the lamp from your real future needs, not a fixed assumption on this page. The Arkan blade requires <strong>60 Attack</strong> and offers useful stab/slash and a special attack, but its <strong>64 Strength bonus</strong> is slightly below the dragon scimitar's 66; it is <em>not</em> a universal replacement. No post-quest Delve farm is required. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Arkan_blade" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Blade stats</a>. <strong>Claim the 25,000 RC XP before Step 11.</strong></p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i32-rc-55" number="11" title="Reach actual 55 Runecraft after The Final Dawn">
        <p>Read live RC XP after the <strong>25,000-XP</strong> reward. At the exact-52 stop, <strong>123,660 + 25,000 = 148,660 XP</strong>. Actual 55 begins at <strong>166,636 XP</strong>; the conservative remainder is <strong>17,976 XP</strong>. Train only that live remainder. <strong>The Fremennik Exiles</strong> consumes actual 55 and immediately awards another 30,000 RC XP, so do not train to the later level-60 gate now.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Fremennik finale</div><h2>Three deliberate gates, one large reward bundle.</h2></section>
      <div class="callout"><strong>Before leaving for Rellekka:</strong> verify actual <strong>55 Runecraft, 60 Slayer, 65 Crafting, 60 Smithing, 60 Fishing and 60 Mining</strong> in the live skill tab. Only the first three needed deliberate work here; Chapter 2 exceeds the others. Check The Fremennik Isles, Lunar Diplomacy, Mountain Daughter and Heroes' Quest (with their chains) in the quest journal. These are a preflight for Step 12, not extra progress checkboxes.</div>
      <RouteStep id="i32-exiles" number="12" title="Complete The Fremennik Exiles; record post-quest XP">
        <p><strong>Before speaking to Brundt</strong> in the Rellekka Longhall, buy <strong>two kegs of beer</strong> from Thora; her Rellekka stock is not available during the exile phase. Stage the other items by phase: a <strong>mirror shield</strong> and one-handed combat weapon for the early basilisk; <strong>pet rock</strong> (reclaim from Askeladden if missing), <strong>ice gloves and fishing rod</strong> for the Mountain Camp geyser; and <strong>one molten glass, 100 astral runes, seal of passage, pickaxe, hammer and glassblowing pipe</strong> for Lunar Isle's lunar glass, three lunar bars and the restored V's shield. Bring food, Prayer restores and a teleport for combat. Bank between the Rellekka, Mountain Camp and Lunar phases rather than carrying all of this at once. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Fremennik_Exiles" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current item and fight guide</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Do not confuse the required Fremennik shield with the Neitiznot shield.</strong> Bank-check the untradeable Fremennik shield first. If absent, after the quest exiles you, take Jarvald's boat to Waterbirth Island and obtain one <em>without a drop roll</em> from <strong>Bardur</strong> deep in the dungeon: buy about <strong>5–10 rune thrownaxes</strong> from the Ranging Guild's Tribal Weapon Salesman (the route clears its 40-Ranged entry), take your pet rock, combat gear, food and Prayer, put the rock on one floor plate and stand on the other, then use the thrownaxe special attack on the western door supports to open the lower route. Bardur gives a shield free once with an activated <strong>ring of charos(a)</strong>, or sells it for <strong>150,000 coins</strong>. A random shield from dagannoths/market guards also works, but no drop is assumed. The shield, lunar glass, enchanted V sigil and polishing rock become <strong>V's shield</strong> with a glassblowing pipe. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Waterbirth_Island_Dungeon" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Solo dungeon route</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Jormungand primer:</strong> wear the quest-made <strong>V's shield</strong>; without it, the fight's stat drain and repeated damage are severe. A dragon mace is an attainable crush option against its slight crush weakness, with ordinary defensive melee gear and Piety. <strong>Protect from Magic</strong> greatly reduces regular magic damage but does not make you invulnerable. When the screen turns red, <strong>face away</strong> from Jormungand to avoid the gaze/drain; if encased in stone, repeatedly attempt to attack to break free before the large delayed hit. Bring enough food and restore doses for a multi-minute fight; teleporting out is safer than gambling a low-supply finish. A death/teleport restarts the Jormungand fight (not the whole quest), and Brundt handles item recovery on the island. No RNG weapon is a prerequisite.</p>
        <p>Claim <strong>50,000 Slayer, 50,000 Crafting and 30,000 Runecraft XP</strong>, V's shield and Island of Stone access. The quest unlocks Basilisk Knights on task and the <strong>Neitiznot faceguard</strong> upgrade path, but the basilisk jaw is an RNG drop; keep using the already-owned Helm of Neitiznot and <strong>do not camp a jaw</strong>. At exact prequest floors, Slayer <strong>273,742 + 50,000 = 323,742 XP</strong> (at least level 61), Crafting <strong>449,428 + 50,000 = 499,428 XP</strong> (at least level 66), and Runecraft <strong>166,636 + 30,000 = 196,636 XP</strong> (at least level 56). Write down the <em>actual</em> post-quest levels/XP for later pages. Do not immediately grind Slayer 69, Crafting 70 or Runecraft 60.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">3.2 complete · mandatory exit only</div>
        <h3>Quest XP has done its work; stop at the real boundary.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Complete:</strong> Perilous Moons (including one normal Lunar Chest reward), The Heart of Darkness, Fallen From Grace, Devious Minds, The Final Dawn and The Fremennik Exiles.</li>
          <li><strong>Measured gates before consumers:</strong> Slayer 60, Runecraft 47 → 50 → 52 → 55, and Crafting 65. Fallen's Crafting/RC, Devious Minds' RC and Final Dawn's RC rewards landed before each following training interval.</li>
          <li><strong>Now banked/unlocked:</strong> Wyrmscraig and Tapoyauik access, Island of Stone, V's shield, Arkan blade, and Exiles' additional 50,000 Slayer / 50,000 Crafting / 30,000 Runecraft XP. Record live XP before the next page.</li>
          <li><strong>Not guaranteed:</strong> Moon armour or atlatl, Hallowfell, Mad Angel drops, black mask/Slayer helmet, basilisk jaw/faceguard, Bowfa/crystal, Fire Cape, Runecraft 60, Slayer 69 or Crafting 70.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <div class="subchapter-pager"><a class="button secondary" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-1/`}>← 3.1</a><a class="button secondary" href={`${base}intermediate/`}>Back to Intermediate overview</a></div>
    </article>
